TWEAK_NAME="Audio stack profiler"
TWEAK_RISK="low"
TWEAK_EXPERIMENTAL=1
TWEAK_DESCRIPTION="Installs a read-only runtime into /data/opencmu/boot.d that watches the audio stack after boot: it finds the lastModeSvc process and its -f persistence file via /proc, watches that file for changes, polls the stock audio ready flags (/var/run/audio_start and the four /tmp/dbus entries from sm.conf), and runs a passive dbus-monitor on the com.jci.vbs.vdt and com.jci.vbs.bcm broadcast signals. It calls no getters, never touches smdb-read, starts and stops nothing, and writes only its own log. Requires 60-startup-hook."
